---
import Prose from './Prose.astro';
import CodeBlock from './CodeBlock.astro';
import { API_FAILURES, API_TRIAGE } from '../data/guide';

const errorExample = `// response body on failure
{ "success": false, "code": "BRAND_IN_USE", "message": "Brand has products" }

// client — branch on the stable code, not the message
switch (err.code) {
  case 'BRAND_IN_USE':
    return setFieldError('brand', 'Remove its products first');
  default:
    return toast(err.message); // human-facing fallback only
}`;
---

<Prose class="max-w-none">
  <h3>Tools</h3>
  <p>
    Most API problems are visible in the browser DevTools Network tab: the status code, the timing
    waterfall, request and response headers, the request payload and the response body. Filter to
    Fetch/XHR, turn on Preserve log so requests survive a navigation, and use Copy as cURL to replay
    a request outside the app.
  </p>
  <p>
    RTK Query and React Query both ship devtools that show cache entries, their tags, and what
    triggered a refetch — the fastest way to explain stale or missing data. MSW (Mock Service
    Worker) lets you reproduce a specific failing response deterministically inside a test.
  </p>

  <h3>Reading a response</h3>
  <p>
    Every TechCart response has the same shape: success, code and message. On failure, branch the UI
    on code, which is a stable string; treat message as a human-facing fallback and never parse it
    for logic.
  </p>
  <CodeBlock title="error handling" code={errorExample} />

  <h3>Common failures</h3>
  <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-border">
    <table class="w-full border-collapse text-left text-sm">
      <thead class="bg-surface text-xs tracking-wide text-muted uppercase">
        <tr>
          <th class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Symptom</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Likely cause</th>
          <th class="px-4 py-2 font-medium">Fix</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {API_FAILURES.map((row) => (
          <tr class="border-t border-border align-top">
            <td class="px-4 py-2 font-medium text-fg">{row.symptom}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted">{row.cause}</td>
            <td class="px-4 py-2 text-muted">{row.fix}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h3>Triage flow</h3>
  <ol>
    {API_TRIAGE.map((step) => (
      <li>{step}</li>
    ))}
  </ol>
</Prose>
